      <div type="clause" n="12">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IICn">II Cn</ref> 12</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="12" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="316" ed="#liebermann"/>Ðis syndon þa gerihta<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#IICn_12.lnote.oe.9"/>, þe se cingc<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#IICn_12.lnote.oe.10"/> ah ofer ealle men on Wessexan<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#IICn_12.lnote.oe.11"/>: þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> is<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#IICn_12.lnote.oe.12"/> mundbryce ⁊ hamsocne, forsteal<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#IICn_12.lnote.oe.13"/> ⁊<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="†" target="#IICn_12.lnote.oe.dagger"/> flymena fyrmðe ⁊ fyrdwite, butan he<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#IICn_12.lnote.oe.8-3"/> hwæne ðe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="*" target="#IICn_12.lnote.oe.star"/> furðor gemæðrian wylle<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#IICn_12.lnote.oe.14"/> (⁊<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="**" target="#IICn_12.lnote.oe.star2-2"/> he him ðæs weorðscipes geunne).</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="12" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="316" ed="#liebermann"/>Ðis syndon ða gerihta, ðe se cyning ah ofer ealle men on Wessexan: þæt is mundbryce ⁊ hamsocne, forstal ⁊ fyrdwite, buton hwǽne he furðor gemæðian wylle.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="12" corresp="#wit-a"><pb n="316" ed="#liebermann"/>Þis syndon þa geriht<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IICn_12.lnote.oe.4-3"/>, þe se cyningc ah ofer ealle menn<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#IICn_12.lnote.oe.5-3"/> Westseaxan: þæt is mundbrice ⁊ hamsocne, forestal ⁊ fyrdigce<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#IICn_12.lnote.oe.6-3"/>, buton he hwæne furðor mæðrian wylle.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="12" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="317" ed="#liebermann"/>Hęc sunt iura, quę rex habet super omnes homines in <ptr type="liebermannNote" n="**" target="#IICn_12.lnote.oe.star2"/>Mircenis<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IICn_12.lnote.oe.4-2"/> et Westsexa: mundbrece<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#IICn_12.lnote.oe.5-2"/> (id est infractionem pacis), hámsocnam (id est inuasionem mansionis), foresteal<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#IICn_12.lnote.oe.6-2"/> (id est prohibitionem itineris) et fyrdunga<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#IICn_12.lnote.oe.7-2"/> (id est expeditionem), nisi aliquem<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#IICn_12.lnote.oe.8-2"/> amplius honorare uelit.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="12" corresp="#wit-inst-cn"><pb n="317" ed="#liebermann"/>Hę<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_12.lnote.oe.1"/> sunt consuetudines<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_12.lnote.oe.2-2"/> regis, quas<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_12.lnote.oe.3-2"/> habet super<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IICn_12.lnote.oe.4-4"/> omnes homines in Westsexe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#IICn_12.lnote.oe.5-4"/>: forisfacturam, quam Angli uocant mundbrece<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#IICn_12.lnote.oe.6-4"/>, hamsocne<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#IICn_12.lnote.oe.7-3"/>, hoc<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#IICn_12.lnote.oe.8-4"/> est inuasio in propria domo aut infra curiam causa<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#IICn_12.lnote.oe.9-2"/> alicuius mali, foresteal<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#IICn_12.lnote.oe.10-2"/>, quod nos possumus dicere contrastationem<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#IICn_12.lnote.oe.11-2"/>, causa mali; ferdƿite<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#IICn_12.lnote.oe.12-2"/>, quod nos possumus dicere dimissionem belli; hę sunt<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#IICn_12.lnote.oe.13-2"/>, inquam, consuetudines regis, nisi rex uelit aliquem honorare, dando ei quod sui iuris est.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="12" corresp="#wit-cons-cn"><pb n="317" ed="#liebermann"/>De iure domini regis. Hee sunt rectitudines, quas rex habet super omnes homines in Westsexia; que sunt: monte fractura, domi inuasio, obstitus, exercitus reatus, nisi cui rex misereri uoluerit.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="12" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="180" ed="#robertson"/>Ðis syndon ða gerihta ðe se cyning ah ofer ealle men on Wessexan, þæt is mundbryce ⁊ hamsocne, forstal<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#IICn_12.robnote.fn.2"/> ⁊ fyrdwite<ptr type="editorNote" n="3" target="#IICn_12.robnote.fn.3"/>, buton hwǽne h<ptr type="editorNote" n="4" target="#IICn_12.robnote.fn.4"/>e furðor gemæðia<ptr type="editorNote" n="5" target="#IICn_12.robnote.fn.5"/>n wyll<ptr type="editorNote" n="6" target="#IICn_12.robnote.fn.6"/>e.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="258" ed="#rabin-doml"/>Ðis syndon þa gerihta þe se cingc ah ofer ealle men on Wessexan: þæt is mundbryce and hamsocne, forsteal and flymena fyrmðe and fyrdwite, butan he hwæne ðe furðor gemæðrian wylle and he him ðæs weorðscipes geunne.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="316" ed="#liebermann"/>Dies<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_12.lnote.de.1"/> sind die<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_12.lnote.de.2"/> [Jurisdictions]gerechtsame<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_12.lnote.de.3"/>, die der König über alle<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IICn_12.lnote.de.4"/> Leute in Wessex [vorbehalten] hat: nämlich den<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#IICn_12.lnote.de.5"/> Bruch der [besonderen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#IICn_12.lnote.de.6"/> königlichen] Schutzgewalt<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#IICn_12.lnote.de.7"/> und [unerlaubte] Heimsuchung<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#IICn_12.lnote.de.8"/>, Wegsperrung<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#IICn_12.lnote.de.9"/> (und Beherbergung Geächteter<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#IICn_12.lnote.de.10"/> <hi rend="italic">G</hi>) und Strafe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#IICn_12.lnote.de.11"/> für Heer[versäumniss], ausser wenn er jemanden (um so <hi rend="italic">G</hi>) weiter<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#IICn_12.lnote.de.12"/> ehren<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#IICn_12.lnote.de.13"/> will (indem er ihm die Jurisdictionswürde [auch hierüber] verleiht <hi rend="italic">G</hi>).</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">These are the [jurisdictional] rights which the king has [reserved] over all men in Wessex: namely breach of [his special] protection, and [unlawful] attack on a house, obstruction (and harbouring outlaws, G), and the fine for [neglect of] military service, unless he wishes to honour someone further (by granting him the jurisdiction [over these too], G).</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="181" ed="#robertson"/>These are the dues<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IICn_12.robnote.n.1"/> to which the king is entitled from all men in Wessex, namely, [the payments for] violation of his <hi rend="italic">mund<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#IICn_12.robnote.n.2"/></hi>, and for attacks on people's houses, for assault<ptr type="editorNote" n="3" target="#IICn_12.robnote.n.3"/> and for neglecting military service<ptr type="editorNote" n="4" target="#IICn_12.robnote.n.4"/>, unless he desires to show especial honour to anyone [by granting him these dues]<ptr type="editorNote" n="5" target="#IICn_12.robnote.n.5"/>.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="463" ed="#whitelock"/>These are the rights which the king possesses over all men in Wessex, namely <hi rend="italic">mundbryce<ptr type="editorNote" n="3" target="#IICn_12.whinote.n.3"/></hi> and <hi rend="italic">hamsocn</hi>,<ptr type="editorNote" n="4" target="#IICn_12.whinote.n.4"/> <hi rend="italic">forstal<ptr type="editorNote" n="5" target="#IICn_12.whinote.n.5"/></hi> and [the fine for] the harbouring of fugitives<ptr type="editorNote" n="6" target="#IICn_12.whinote.n.6"/> and the fine for neglecting military service, unless he wishes to honour anyone further.<ptr type="editorNote" n="7" target="#IICn_12.whinote.n.7"/></ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="259" ed="#rabin-doml"/>These are the fines to which the king is entitled from all the people of Wessex: that is, fines for the violation of the king’s protection and for home invasion, for assault, harboring of fugitives, and shirking military service, unless he wishes to specially privilege someone by allocating these fines to him.</ab>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#liebermann"><ref target="clause:IICn_14">II Cn 14</ref>; <ref target="clause:LeisWl_2">Leis Wl 2</ref></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-ppmel" n="204"><ref target="clause:Hn_10-1">Hn 10.1</ref></note>
        <note type="editorial">G's ‘⁊ flymena fyrmðe’ is missing from the other MSS and not original; G's ‘ðe’ (also in 15) and ‘(⁊ he him ðæs weorðscipes geunne)’ are perhaps not original either (Liebermann). A's ‘fyrdigce’ should be ‘fyrdinge’. Quadr. includes Mercia (‘Mircenis’), drawn forward from 14.; BR: added from Gesetze I p. 317, October 2026 (MS Cons); AP: corrected against Whitelock p. 463, October 2026 (was “These are the rights which the king possesses over all men in Wessex, namely mundbryce and hamsocn, forstal and [the fine for] the harbouring of fugitives and the fine for neglecting military service, unless he wishes to honour anyone further.”, now “These are the rights which the king possesses over all men in Wessex, namely mundbryce and hamsocn, forstal and [the fine for] the harbouring of fugitives and the fine for neglecting military service, unless he wishes to honour anyone further. (expanded letters in italics: mundbryce, hamsocn, forstal)”)</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">and flymena fyrmðe: omitted AB</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">and he . . . geunne: omitted AB</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_12.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">317</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">He <hi rend="italic">Hk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">He Hk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_12.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">317</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">in W. s. o.; que <hi rend="italic">Hk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">in W. s. o.; que Hk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_12.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">317</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Wessessia <hi rend="italic">Hr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Wessessia Hr</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_12.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">317</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">monete <hi rend="italic">Hr;</hi> monefactura <hi rend="italic">Hk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">monete Hr; monefactura Hk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_12.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">317</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">obsitus <hi rend="italic">Hk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">obsitus Hk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_12.lnote.oe.7" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">317</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">r. e. <hi rend="italic">Hk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">r. e. Hk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_12.lnote.oe.8" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">317</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">quid <hi rend="italic">Hr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">quid Hr</seg></note>
